# Production build values for the frontend (PLAN.md §18).
#
# Committed on purpose: these are public origin URLs, not secrets, and they must agree
# with the worker's ALLOWED_ORIGINS in apps/signaling-worker/wrangler.toml. A mismatch
# fails in one of two ways, both silent-ish: the browser blocks the session-mint fetch
# (CORS/CSP), or the QR encodes an origin that nothing is served on. The dev origin guard
# in pages/Home.tsx catches the second case in development builds.
#
# When the custom domain replaces pages.dev, change BOTH this file and ALLOWED_ORIGINS.

# Base WebSocket URL of the deployed signaling worker.
VITE_SIGNALING_URL=wss://qrdrop-signaling.proyas.workers.dev

# Public origin this app is served from; every QR code encodes it.
# NOT qrdrop.pages.dev: that hostname is claimed by an unrelated account (verified by
# fetching it — it serves a stock Vite scaffold whose title never appears in this repo's
# git history). Workers static assets under our own subdomain is verifiably ours.
VITE_APP_URL=https://qrdrop-app.proyas.workers.dev
